# The repo-root .gitignore ignores `Cargo.lock` globally (root-workspace crates lock via the seed root).
# But cdz-wasm is its OWN [workspace] (root-excluded — it's the browser-facing wasm-bindgen wrapper built
# for wasm32 by wasm-pack, never part of the native seed build), so it needs its OWN Cargo.lock to build
# reproducibly offline. The full-CI-in-nix arc (v-nix) nixifies the guide-examples job, which runs
# `wasm-pack build` on this crate in a hermetic derivation that can only vendor from a git-tracked lock.
# So we COMMIT this crate's Cargo.lock — un-ignore it here (scoped to this dir) — mirroring the
# cedar-policy-guest / reducer-guest fixtures. `--locked` builds are then deterministic in CI + Nix.
!Cargo.lock

# `wasm-pack build --target web` emits a pkg/ dir here (the guide stages it into guide/src/wasm/pkg/,
# already git-ignored). It's build output — never commit it; ignore so a direct in-crate build stays clean.
pkg/
